this morning we're taking a look at life  inside the largest resettlement complex  for evacuees who fled afghanistan after  the taliban takeover it's called fort  mccoy it's an army post in wisconsin and  one of eight military bases taking part  in operation allies welcome it provides  nearly 13 000 afghans with medical care  and support to build their lives in the  united states in an exclusive interview  nancy chen spoke to one family of seven  who left their world behind and are now  starting over nancy good morning  tony good morning to you the first  evacuees arrived here nearly six weeks  ago it is one of eight military  installations across the country housing  those who have left afghanistan families  are working now to adjust to their new  lives and new realities  there is gratitude and hope for families  starting a new life and getting their  chance at achieving the american dream  it was so hard to leave our home our  country nineteen-year-old sultana amani  arrived in the u.s in late august with  her family after fleeing afghanistan  under taliban rule you never would have  wanted to leave otherwise i was happy  there but  when the tall one came we were in danger  surrounded by miles of farmland and  cornfields this is where the amani  family is starting their life in the u.s  this initiative follows through on  america's commitment to afghan personnel  who helped us about half the evacuees  housed here are children who take  english classes  craft art projects and kick soccer balls  however there is sadness for what they  left behind sultana's father muhammad  naimamani  i worked for 40 years  and seeing everything goes to waste i  seeing the kids seeing the woman going  everything  backwards i feel really bad and i feel  sad about it  but with despair there is the drive to  make a difference back home i hope in  the future  i changed some  somethings people liked all about  i hope to change them so you don't want  to just  change life here  you want to change life in afghanistan  in the future there is a hope only her  mom khadijah rahimi dreams of their  family giving back to the country that  took them in  yeah i'm very happy to be here that my  kids are here they will have a bright  future and i hope in future they will  make this place even a better place what  do you hope for  at the end of all this  i want peace  i just don't want only peace for my own  family that we are in us i want peace  and security for my afghans who are  there who are left behind  now families are expected to resettle  across the country but the exact  timeline for that is unclear at this  point by the way there have been eight  deliveries so far on base including a  set of twins all are american citizens  dana  new hope for the future nancy thank you  very much
 

